1. **Avoid double padding in `tensorflow/compiler/tf2xla/kernels/light_outside_compilation.cc`:**
   `BufferSize` (lines 438-439) returns the 4-byte-padded size for outputs, and `WriteIntoXlaBufferAllocator::AllocateRaw` (lines 400-401) pads `buffer_size_` a second time. Meanwhile, input allocators (lines 679 and 694) still store the unpadded `input_size`. Revert `BufferSize` to `return num_elems * DataTypeSize(descr.type());` so `buffer_size_` always holds the unpadded XLA buffer size. Round `buffer_size_` once in `WriteIntoXlaBufferAllocator::AllocateRaw` with a short comment noting that XLA GPU buffers are aligned well beyond 4 bytes:

