2. **Guard sub-32-bit padding with `if constexpr` in `tensorflow/core/framework/typed_allocator.h`:**
   In `Allocate<T>` (lines 91-99) and `Deallocate<T>` (lines 113-118), `raw_allocator->AllocatesOpaqueHandle()` runs even when `sizeof(T) >= sizeof(uint32_t)`. Calling `AllocationBytes<T>` also repeats the multiplication overflow check from line 87, and `raw_allocator &&` is redundant before an unconditional dereference. Guard the padding block with `if constexpr (sizeof(T) < sizeof(uint32_t))` and call `RoundUpSub32Bit(num_bytes, sizeof(T))` directly:

   ```cpp
       size_t num_bytes = sizeof(T) * num_elements;
       if constexpr (sizeof(T) < sizeof(uint32_t)) {
         if (!raw_allocator->AllocatesOpaqueHandle()) {
           num_bytes = RoundUpSub32Bit(num_bytes, sizeof(T));
           if (num_elements > 0 && num_bytes == 0) {
             return nullptr;
           }
         }
       }
   ```

   Use the same `if constexpr (sizeof(T) < sizeof(uint32_t))` guard in `Deallocate<T>`.

3. **Document `element_size = 1` on `TypedAllocator::RoundUpSub32Bit` in `tensorflow/core/framework/typed_allocator.h`:**
   `ScopedAllocator::AllocateRaw` and `WriteIntoXlaBufferAllocator::AllocateRaw` pass `element_size = 1` to `RoundUpSub32Bit` to round raw byte counts. Note in the `RoundUpSub32Bit` comment (lines 36-38) that callers with a raw byte count can pass `element_size = 1` to round up unconditionally. Alternatively, extract a dedicated `RoundUpTo4Bytes(size_t bytes)` helper.

4. **Strengthen assertions in `ScopedAllocatorMgrTest.Sub32BitOddElements` (`tensorflow/core/common_runtime/scoped_allocator_mgr_test.cc`):**
   Use `ASSERT_NE(nullptr, ptr0)` and `ASSERT_NE(nullptr, ptr1)` (lines 268 and 275) before passing `ptr0` and `ptr1` to `DeallocateRaw`. Also add `EXPECT_EQ(nullptr, sa_instances_[0]->AllocateRaw(0, 7));` before allocating `ptr0` to check that an intermediate byte count is rejected.

5. **Update the pull request description:**
   The commit message matches the current code, but the pull request description still describes the earlier `ScopedAllocatorMgr::PopulateFields` padding approach. Update the PR description so it matches the commit message.
